  "notes": "Both venvs rebuilt with Python 3.13 (the project needs 3.13+); installed fusepy in both and the libfuse2t64 system library. The workload runs on SQLite (no pooling, like the project; files on /dev/shm with disk sync off). It covers single and batch cache writes, which on head also update file_paths sizes. It calls get_content_size on the HN connector, on the S3 connector (in-memory stand-in for the AWS client) and on the Gmail connector (all entries cached). It runs NexusFS.sync_mount on an S3 connector mount (single files, then the whole mount) and FUSE getattr over an in-memory filesystem. The digest differs by design: head returns sizes from the cache, base returns a 10 KB estimate for HN and reads file content in FUSE getattr. In head, the size lookup in sync_mount imports the non-existent nexus.core.operation_context; the error is caught, so sizes stay 0 there. With the default connection pool, head's unclosed sessions exhaust it and the run hangs. check.py passes: head coverage 0.81, base 6.6 s, head 9.1 s, no network."
 },
